---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="API keys and browser tools">
  <h1>API keys and browser tools</h1>

  <h2>Create an API key</h2>
  <p>Public report lookups do not require an API key during the community preview. URL submission is also anonymous. Keys for bulk access and higher limits are not issued yet because a browser-visible key would not protect the service.</p>
  <button type="button" disabled>API key creation coming later</button>
  <p class="muted">When managed API access launches, keys will be shown once, stored only as hashes, scoped, rate-limited, and revocable.</p>

  <h2>Public lookup API</h2>
  <pre><code>GET https://termsinator.46-62-240-211.sslip.io/api/v1/sites/example.com/summary</code></pre>
  <p>The endpoint returns only published report data. Public read responses allow cross-origin access for the bookmarklet.</p>

  <h2>Bookmarklet</h2>
  <p>Drag this link to your bookmarks bar. Clicking it sends only the current hostname to Termsinator and shows a small result panel on the page. Some websites block bookmarklets through their security policy.</p>
  <p><a id="bookmarklet" class="button-link" href="#">Check with Termsinator</a></p>

  <h2>Browser extension</h2>
  <p>The Manifest V3 extension defaults to click-only lookup. Automatic hostname checks and the small page overlay require explicit opt-in. It never sends paths, page titles, or page content.</p>
  <p><a class="button-link" href="/downloads/termsinator-extension.zip" download>Download extension</a> <a href="https://github.com/PAndreew/termsinator/tree/service-poc/extension" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View source on GitHub</a></p>
  <ol>
    <li>Download and unzip the file.</li>
    <li>Open the browser's extensions page and enable developer mode.</li>
    <li>Choose “Load unpacked” and select the unzipped folder.</li>
  </ol>

  <script is:inline type="module">
    const link = document.querySelector('#bookmarklet');
    fetch('/bookmarklet.js')
      .then(response => response.text())
      .then(source => { if (link) link.href = `javascript:${source.trim()}`; })
      .catch(() => { if (link) link.textContent = 'Bookmarklet unavailable'; });
  </script>
</Base>
